# 📚 SOTA Reference: Agent-Native & Human Documentation Engines (Fumadocs vs Fern)

## 1. Ecosystem Baseline & Benchmark Audit (2026)

### A. Fern (fern-api) — Status & Legacy Patterns
- **Repository Status:** `github.com/fern-api/fern` is officially marked unmaintained/archived in open source; the platform transitioned to proprietary cloud-hosted SaaS (`buildwithfern.com`).
- **Core Valuable Patterns:**
  - **Spec-First API Explorer:** 3-column interactive layout (Navigation -> Endpoint Spec & Parameters -> Request/Response Playground with multi-language code snippets: cURL, TypeScript, Python).
  - **RBAC & Audience Gating:** Segmenting documentation by audience (`public`, `customer`, `internal/agent`) to prevent internal schema leakage.
- **Architectural Pitfall:** Direct dependency on legacy Fern OSS CLI creates deprecation lock-in and broken toolchains.

### B. Fumadocs (fuma-nama) — SOTA Standard
- **Repository Status:** Active, permissively licensed (MIT), modular React 19 / Next.js App Router framework.
- **Key Capabilities:**
  - `fumadocs-core`: Page tree navigation, MDX/TOC AST parsing, Shiki highlighting, Zod schema validation.
  - `fumadocs-openapi`: Direct generation of type-safe MDX documentation and interactive test runners from OpenAPI 3.0/3.1 specs.
  - `fumadocs-ui`: Modern Tailwind-based documentation primitives (`<Steps>`, `<Tabs>`, `<Cards>`, `<Callout>`).
  - **Native Agent Integration:**
    - `fumadocs-core/source/llms` & `remark-llms`: Automatic generation of `/llms.txt` and raw markdown routes.
    - `@modelcontextprotocol/server` (MCP): Native MCP endpoints enabling autonomous AI coding agents (Hermes, Claude Code, Cursor) to search and query docs via tool calls.
  - **Instant Search:** Client-side zero-latency search using Orama (WASM) or Flexsearch without third-party SaaS dependencies.

