## 2. Dual-Optics Architecture (Human + Agent Invariants)

Modern documentation must serve two distinct primary consumers without compromising either:

| Consumer | Primary Interface | Latency/Format Requirements | Key Primitives |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Human Developer** | Web UI (Fumadocs App) | Visual clarity, interactive forms, search, responsive theme | MDX components, OpenAPI Explorer, Diátaxis 4-Quadrant guides |
| **AI Agent** | MCP Server / `/llms.txt` | Sub-50ms token-efficient retrieval, zero HTML/DOM slop | Structured MRH headers, plain markdown dumps, JSON Schemas |

### Dual-Optics Invariants:
1. **Zero-Trace Agent Consumption:** Agents must access documentation via `/llms.txt` (summary index $\le$ 2,000 tokens), `/llms-full.txt`, or direct MCP tool queries, never by parsing rendered HTML DOM.
2. **Deterministic Contract Grounding:** API documentation is never written manually; it is compiled synchronously from Pydantic models or OpenAPI JSON (`fumadocs-openapi`).
3. **Machine-Readable Headers (MRH):** Every conceptual markdown page maintains a top-level MRH header (`mrh_id`, `purpose`, `status`, `version`, `author`).

